[size=5][b]Hotkey Customizer[/b][/size]

Add key combinations to vanilla shortcuts, ten user-configurable building shortcuts, and a vertical building hotbar to Kingdom Inc. Every entry starts Unassigned, and your existing workspace shortcuts stay unchanged.

[b]Features[/b]
[list]
[*]Rebind vanilla shortcuts to combinations such as Ctrl + Shift + 1.[/*]
[*]Ten building entries numbered 0-9 in Options > Key Bindings > Custom Hotkeys.[/*]
[*]Building dropdowns on the left; vanilla-style key setters on the right.[/*]
[*]Assign your own key, with optional Ctrl, Alt, Shift or Meta modifiers.[/*]
[*]Choose a specific building from a dropdown for each entry.[/*]
[*]Apply saves assignments; Cancel discards edits; Reset clears the pending entries.[/*]
[*]Opens normal building placement with the game's research and cost checks.[/*]
[*]Settings persist across restarts and kingdoms without adding save data.[/*]
[*]Vertical hotbar at the right edge: hover to reveal, move away to retract. Black backgrounds with native building icons; names appear in hover tooltips.[/*]
[*]Show Hotbar checkbox with Apply/Cancel. Keyboard shortcuts work with the bar hidden. Click icons for normal placement.[/*]
[/list]

[b]How to use[/b]
Open Options > Key Bindings. Click any vanilla key field to assign a combination. For building entries, scroll to Custom Hotkeys and Building 0-9, choose a building on the left and assign a key on the right. Hold modifiers and press the final key, then Apply. Backspace or Delete clears a key during capture. Entry numbers are labels; no number keys are assigned automatically. Avoid shortcuts already used by the game.

[b]Requirements[/b]
Windows Mono Kingdom Inc. and BepInEx 5 with its bundled Harmony. BepInEx is not included.

[b]Installation and removal[/b]
Close the game and extract the archive into its installation folder. The DLL belongs at BepInEx/plugins/HotkeyCustomizer/HotkeyCustomizer.dll. Update only that DLL with the game closed. Remove its plugin folder to uninstall. The optional configuration file is BepInEx/config/urakka.kingdominc.hotkeycustomizer.cfg. No save migration is required. Removing the plugin makes vanilla combinations fall back to their final keys; use Reset to default if desired.

[b]Limitations[/b]
Locked buildings cannot be placed until researched. Hotkeys are suspended during text entry, pause menus, alerts and incompatible tools.

[b]Compatibility[/b]
Existing game shortcuts remain active. Assigning the same key to a building shortcut and a native action can trigger both. When building entries share a shortcut, the lowest-numbered entry takes priority.

Other replacements for the key-binding menu, key capture or input-binding persistence may interfere. The table lists potential patch overlaps; sharing a method does not by itself establish a conflict.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Class.Method[/b][/td][td][b]May conflict with[/b][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]KeyBindingsUI.OnEnable[/td][td]Key-binding menu replacements that override pending settings, saved combinations or the Cancel snapshot.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]KeyBindingsUI.RefreshBindings[/td][td]Key-binding menu replacements that rebuild the row list or remove the custom building entries.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]KeyBindingsUI.ApplyBindings[/td][td]Binding-save replacements that bypass custom assignments or overwrite modifier combinations.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]KeyBindingsUI.ResetBindings[/td][td]Reset-button replacements that bypass clearing the custom building entries and pending bindings.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]KeyBindingsUI.Apply[/td][td]Input-binding loaders that overwrite the saved modifier combinations after loading game controls.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]KeyBindingRow.OnPointerClick[/td][td]Shortcut-capture replacements that consume the same click or start a competing key-capture operation.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]KeyBindingRow._resetBindingText[/td][td]Binding-label replacements that overwrite the displayed key combination.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]GameUI.Start[/td][td]Gameplay UI replacements that remove or cover the building hotbar.[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[b]Credits[/b]
Urakka; BepInEx and Harmony. Native game UI is reused at runtime. No game assets or assemblies are bundled.

